ITEMS = ((('what should i do if a child is choking', 'how do i help a child who is choking during child choking', 'what is the first aid for choking in children', 'how to respond when a young child is choking', 'what to do when a child cannot breathe from choking', 'how do you assist a choking child', 'what helps a child choking on food', 'how can i help a choking child safely', 'what is the best response to child choking', 'how should i handle choking in a young child'), 'If a child is choking and cannot cough or breathe, give firm back blows and check after each one. If the blockage remains, a trained responder may use abdominal thrusts. Call emergency services if the airway does not clear, and learn the technique on a first-aid course.'), (('how do i know if a child is choking for a choking child', 'what are the signs of choking in children', 'how to tell if a child is choking or coughing', 'what does a choking child look like', 'can a child choke and still make noise', 'how to recognise choking in a young child', 'what sounds indicate child choking', 'how do i know when choking in children is severe', 'what if a child can talk while choking', 'how to spot a blocked airway in a child'), 'A choking child may grab the throat, struggle to breathe, make a whistling sound or be unable to speak or cry. If they can cough strongly, encourage coughing and keep watching. Call emergency services if breathing is affected or the child becomes quiet and floppy.'), (('how to give back blows to a choking child', 'where to hit a choking child on the back', 'are back blows useful for child choking', 'how to position a child for back blows', 'what is the correct back blow technique for children', 'should i bend a choking child forward', 'how do i support a child while giving back blows', 'what if back blows do not help a choking child', 'can back blows clear choking in children', 'when to use back blows on a choking young child'), 'Lean a choking child forward and give firm back blows between the shoulder blades with the heel of your hand. Check after each blow and stop if the airway clears. Call emergency services if the obstruction stays, and ask a trained person to take over if one is nearby.'), (('how do i do abdominal thrusts on a child', 'when are abdominal thrusts used for children', 'should i give abdominal thrusts to a choking child', 'how to perform thrusts on a young child', 'is it safe to do abdominal thrusts on children', 'what if abdominal thrusts do not clear child choking', 'where do i press for abdominal thrusts on a child', 'can abdominal thrusts hurt a choking child', 'who should learn abdominal thrusts for children', 'how to adapt thrusts for a small child'), 'Abdominal thrusts may be used for a choking child when back blows have failed, with care and only after training. They can bruise, so they are not for a child who is coughing effectively. Call emergency services if the blockage remains and get hands-on instruction.'), (('what if a choking child can still cough', 'should i hit the back if a child is coughing', 'how to handle mild choking in children', 'what to do when a child is choking but breathing', 'should i intervene if a child can cry', 'how to watch a child with mild choking', 'when to escalate a coughing child who is choking', 'what if a child coughs up the object', 'how long to observe after child choking', 'when to call help for a coughing choking child'), 'If a child can cough, cry and speak, encourage them to keep coughing and stay close, as this can clear the airway naturally. Do not give water or food. Call emergency services if the cough becomes silent, breathing is difficult, or the child looks distressed.'), (('what to do if a child chokes on food during child choking', 'how to help a child choking during a meal', 'what if food blocks a child airway', 'how to clear food choking in children', 'should i give water to a child choking on food', 'what is the response to food choking in children', 'can a drink help a child choking on food', 'how to deal with a blocked airway after eating in children', 'when to call help if a child chokes on food', 'what not to do when food causes child choking'), 'Never give water or food to a child choking on food, as it can push the blockage deeper. Encourage coughing if it is effective, otherwise use back blows and call emergency services. Check the mouth only if the object is clearly visible and easy to remove.'), (('what if a choking child becomes unconscious', 'how to handle an unconscious choking child', 'should i start cpr for a choking child', 'what to do when a child collapses while choking', 'how to place an unconscious choking child', 'what if the child stops responding while choking', 'how to check the mouth of an unconscious choking child', 'what happens if choking leads to unconsciousness in children', 'should i call emergency services for an unconscious choking child', 'how to help a collapsed child after choking'), "If a choking child becomes unconscious, call emergency services and begin CPR with rescue breaths if you are trained. Do not sweep the mouth blindly. Keep the child warm and follow the operator's instructions until a qualified person arrives."), (('what if a child with special needs is choking', 'how to help a disabled child who is choking', 'can i do back blows on a child in a wheelchair', 'how to position a child with mobility needs when choking', 'what if i cannot lift a choking child', 'how to adapt choking first aid for children', 'should i ask the child how to help', 'what to do if a child cannot follow instructions', 'how to support a child with a feeding tube who is choking', 'when to get urgent help for a child with extra needs'), "Keep the child in the position that helps them most and give back blows if you can reach their upper back safely. Ask them or their carer what usually helps. Call emergency services if breathing is affected, and explain the child's needs to the operator."), (('should i take a child to hospital after choking', 'what to check after a child choking episode', 'can choking cause injury in children', 'does a child need review after choking clears', 'what symptoms after child choking need review', 'how to settle a child after choking', 'should a young child be checked after choking', 'what if breathing is noisy after child choking', 'when to get checked following choking in children', 'what complications can follow choking in a child'), 'A child who has had difficulty breathing should be checked by a doctor, especially if coughing continues, breathing is noisy or they seem unusually sleepy. Thrusts can cause bruising. Call emergency services if breathing worsens or the child becomes unwell.'), (('when should i call an ambulance for child choking', 'how long do i wait before calling for child choking help', 'is choking in a child always an emergency', 'what if choking will not clear in a child', 'should i call emergency services for mild child choking', 'when to escalate choking in children', 'what if a choking child turns blue', 'how urgent is choking in a young child', 'should i call if a child can still cough', 'what to tell the operator about child choking'), "Call emergency services if a child cannot breathe, speak or cry, or if the blockage does not clear quickly. Give the operator the child's age and say that the airway is blocked. Stay calm, keep giving first aid, and hand over to a qualified person when they arrive."))
